                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've been playing Parkitect for years, the game has steadily gotten better and better through developer updates and a strong modding community, meaning the game rarely becomes stale!\r\n\r\nThe main campaign is fun but not too challenging and can be played through with friends as it supports multiplayer which I adore! Then there's sandbox modes which leave you free to do whatever you like for as long or a little as you like.\r\n\r\nThen there's the addition of custom campaigns, a collection of scenarios made by other players that expand the game massively and give you plenty to go at! Despite my playtime, I wouldn't say I'm the best at the game by any stretch but some of the custom  scenarios will really challenge you. This doesn't feel like padding either, it's just honest to goodness fun and I'd argue it even boarders cozy gaming too as you can play this game really chilled out thanks to the ability to pause simulation and have a break.\r\n\r\nOne of the rides you were expecting to see not in the game? Mods. Want better, more atmospheric lighting? Mods. Coastercam? Mods! There is so much to look at in the base game and even more on the workshop. I can highly recommend Parkitect for those of us who adore Planet Coaster but find it to be a little too in depth! If you enjoyed Rollercoaster Tycoon 2, you'll likely enjoy this too!",
